 # queue-batch
-A small Node library. Run npm test.
+A small Node library. Run `npm test`.
+
+`work(q, send, limit = 1)` sends up to `limit` jobs that were ready when the
+call began, in FIFO order. `limit` must be a nonnegative safe integer. A
+successful job is acknowledged; a failed job is retried once at the ready
+queue tail and is not processed again during the same call. The result has
+`sent` and `retried` ID arrays in processing order. A zero limit or an empty
+queue does nothing.
